From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 29 Jun 2026 16:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] emulationstation: OTA toast says "UPDATING DUCKTALE"

Cosmetic DUCKTALE rebrand: the software-update progress toast titled itself
"UPDATING <getApplicationName()>", and getApplicationName() returns the
hardcoded "ROCKNIX" (kept as-is -- GuiMenu gates the About screen on
`== "ROCKNIX"`). Use the product name in this one toast so a DUCKTALE OTA
reads "UPDATING DUCKTALE". The translatable "UPDATING %s" string is untouched.
---
 es-app/src/guis/GuiUpdate.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiUpdate.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiUpdate.cpp
@@ -21,5 +21,5 @@
 		mWndNotification = mWindow->createAsyncNotificationComponent();
 
-		auto label = Utils::String::format(_("UPDATING %s").c_str(), ApiSystem::getInstance()->getApplicationName().c_str());
+		auto label = Utils::String::format(_("UPDATING %s").c_str(), "DUCKTALE");
 		mWndNotification->updateTitle(_U("\uF019 ") + label);
 
